<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="QueryFlag: Install and activate" id="QueryFlag-Installation">

  <primary-label ref="queryflag"/>
  <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

  <tldr>
    <p>Install: <ui-path>Settings | Plugins | Marketplace</ui-path></p>
    <p>License: 30-day free trial, then <ui-path>Help | Register</ui-path></p>
    <p>Requires: the Database Tools and SQL plugin</p>
  </tldr>

  <link-summary>Check the requirements, install QueryFlag from JetBrains Marketplace, and start the trial or activate a license.</link-summary>
  <card-summary>Check the requirements, install the plugin, and start the trial or activate a license.</card-summary>
  <web-summary>Install the QueryFlag plugin in JetBrains IDEs from JetBrains Marketplace, check its requirements, and start the 30-day trial or activate a license.</web-summary>

  <p>
    Install QueryFlag from JetBrains Marketplace, then start the free trial or activate a license.
  </p>

  <chapter title="Before you begin" id="requirements">
    <list>
      <li>
        The current version requires JetBrains IDEs 2026.3 (build 263) or later.
        For IDE version 2026.2, JetBrains Marketplace offers QueryFlag 2026.2.1.
      </li>
      <li>
        QueryFlag depends on the Database Tools and SQL plugin.
        Use an IDE that includes it, for example IntelliJ IDEA Ultimate or DataGrip, and make sure the plugin is enabled.
        JetBrains Marketplace also lists other IDEs as compatible, for example PyCharm, GoLand, and PhpStorm; they need the Database Tools and SQL plugin, too.
      </li>
      <li>
        To run queries, add at least one data source in the <control>Database</control> tool window (in DataGrip, <control>Database Explorer</control>).
        QueryFlag uses your existing data sources and does not store connection credentials.
      </li>
    </list>
  </chapter>

  <chapter title="Install the plugin" id="install">
    <procedure title="Install QueryFlag from JetBrains Marketplace" id="QueryFlag-installation">
      <step>
        Press <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+S</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ,</shortcut>) to open the <control>Settings</control> dialog,
        and select <control>Plugins</control>.
      </step>
      <step>
        Open the <control>Marketplace</control> tab.
      </step>
      <step>
        Type <code>QueryFlag</code> in the search field.
        <!-- planned-image src="queryflag_install_marketplace.png" alt="Settings dialog, Plugins page, Marketplace tab with QueryFlag in the search results" -->
      </step>
      <step>
        Click <control>Install</control> next to QueryFlag.
      </step>
      <step>
        If the IDE asks for a restart, click <control>Restart IDE</control>.
      </step>
    </procedure>
    <p>
      JetBrains Marketplace installs the QueryFlag build that matches your IDE version.
    </p>
  </chapter>

  <chapter title="Start the trial or activate a license" id="license">
    <p>
      QueryFlag is a paid plugin with a 30-day free trial.
      If you have not started the trial or activated a license yet, the IDE opens the <control>Manage Subscriptions</control> dialog when it starts.
      Start the trial or activate a license there.
      If you close the dialog without doing either, the IDE disables QueryFlag.
      The IDE also disables QueryFlag when the trial or the license expires.
    </p>
    <procedure title="Start the trial or activate a license" id="license-procedure">
      <step>
        Select <ui-path>Help | Register</ui-path>.
      </step>
      <step>
        Select QueryFlag in the list of plugins, and start the trial or activate your license.
      </step>
    </procedure>
    <p>
      Buy or manage licenses on the <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/18269-queryflag/pricing">QueryFlag pricing page</a>.
      The license terms are on the <a href="https://dorkag.com/services-terms-and-conditions">DORKAG terms and conditions</a> page.
    </p>
  </chapter>

  <chapter title="Update the plugin" id="update">
    <procedure title="Update QueryFlag" id="update-queryflag">
      <step>
        Open the <control>Settings</control> dialog and select <control>Plugins</control>.
      </step>
      <step>
        Open the <control>Installed</control> tab, find QueryFlag, and click <control>Update</control> if an update is available.
      </step>
    </procedure>
  </chapter>

  <chapter title="Next steps" id="next-steps">
    <p>
      <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic">Create a query template</a>, then
      <a href="Work-with-QueryFlag.topic">run it on selected text</a>.
    </p>
  </chapter>

